f32 ladders: 64B halves to 32B, narrower widths offer one rung: true
f16 and f64 ladders halve the same way: true
a backend that renders no vectors offers no rungs: true
a long loop takes the full width (517 -> 16 lanes): true
an extent the narrower width divides steps down (40 -> 8 lanes): true
an extent below the wide vector still vectorizes narrow (12 -> 8 lanes): true
an extent below every rung declines (7 -> none): true
the remainder is not chased at scale (1000 -> 16 lanes, not 8): true
a 64-byte register file never renders more trips than a 32-byte one, f32: true
likewise at f16 and f64: true
and strictly fewer on some extents: true
widening never turns a vectorized extent into a serial one: true
